{
  "manufacturer": "Lumel",
  "manufacturer_slug": "lumel",
  "model": "ND20LITE network parameter meter",
  "model_slug": "nd20lite",
  "short_model": "ND20LITE",
  "aliases": [
    "ND20LITE"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Power meter (panel network parameter meter)",
  "applies_to": "Lumel ND20LITE 96x96 panel meter with RS-485 Modbus RTU (not the ND20 or ND20CT, which have their own maps).",
  "summary": "The ND20LITE is a 96x96 panel meter for 3- and 1-phase networks with an RS-485 Modbus RTU port. Measured values are floats offered in several register areas; this map uses the 7000 area (two registers per value, high word first) for per-phase and total values, THD and energies, plus the 4000 area for comms settings, 32-bit energy counters and the status word.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 1,
    "baud": 9600,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 2,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "0-based",
    "note": "Addresses are used as printed: the example frames read 4000 as 0x0FA0, 7000 as 0x1B58 and 6000 as 0x1770. The 'documented' field of float registers shows the table's 6xxx/7xxx pair; this map uses the 7xxx address."
  },
  "default_word_order": "ABCD",
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "ND20LITE Meter of network parameters - User's manual",
    "doc_number": null,
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://www.lumel.com.pl/resources/Pliki%20do%20pobrania/ND20LITE/ND20LITE_user_manual.pdf",
    "pages": "Serial interface and example frames pp. 35-38; Table 8 register areas p. 39; Table 9 (4000 area) pp. 40-44; status bits p. 45; Table 10 floats pp. 47-55 (printed page numbers)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Byte order: the area table gives 7000-7319 as bytes 3-2-1-0 and 6000-6319 as 1-0-3-2; example 2 returns 41 20 00 00 (10.0) from 7000 and example 3 returns 00 00 41 20 from 6000, so the 7000 area is high word first (ABCD).",
    "Energy counters 4038-4047 follow the manual's formula (high x 65536 + low) / 10.",
    "Left out: the min/max area from 7140, 7054 (labelled a phase L1 value inside the 3-phase block), 4057 (its value list prints 3Ph/4W twice), 7120-7138 (reserved, time and 'utilized ordered power' printed with unit V), 7086/7543 which the table skips, the alarm and display setup registers, and 4061 status 2.",
    "Table 10 shows which values exist in 3Ph/4W, 3Ph/3W and 1Ph/2W modes; per-phase values are not valid in 3-wire mode."
  ],
